{"name":"Mysterious Mixture","hex":"#0f521a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mysterious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of unknown origin.","Having unknown qualities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mysterious"},{"term":"mixture","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of mixing.","Something produced by mixing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mixture"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mixture","blocks":[{"text":"In chemistry, a mixture is a material made up of two or more different chemical substances which can be separated by physical method. It is an impure substance made up of two or more elements or compounds mechanically mixed together in any proportion. A mixture is the physical combination of two or more substances in which the identities are retained and are mixed in the form of solutions, suspensions or colloids."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixture","wikidata":"Q169336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mixing_Oil_and_Water.gif/250px-Mixing_Oil_and_Water.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/30/Mixing_Oil_and_Water.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mixing_Oil_and_Water.gif/250px-Mixing_Oil_and_Water.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Making an heterogeneous mixture of water and oil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMixing_Oil_and_Water.gif"}],"sounds":{"mysterious":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/En-us-mysterious.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b0/En-us-mysterio